A||N||16||RickPierce||Someone hit my 85 SE||||8||
Z||000000||RickPierce||01-30-2000||09:51 AM||||Posted this on alt.auto.fiero as well<P>Well this has got to be the most expensive trip to the store that I can<BR>remember.  Got back from a business trip early Saturday morning and after<BR>sleeping in decided it was a nice day to take the Fiero out.  Ran up to the<BR>health food store @ hilltop mall (for those Bay Area owners).  After leaving<BR>was headed for the freeway - came to the four way stop @ Blume Road and<BR>Klose Way and stopped (of course).  Looked left and noticed a green Explorer<BR>was really moving downhill (50-60 in a 35 zone) and said to myself well this<BR>guy isn't going to stop - so just stay where you are.  Sure enough he ran<BR>it - like he never saw it (he was headed to his local bank branch so he had<BR>seen it before).  From then it's all slow motion as I saw him entering into<BR>the intersection a red camry who had stopped, started to turn left to go in<BR>the direction where I came from, in front of the explorer - full on<BR>broadside, the camry and the Explorer bounced around and the camry was<BR>sliding towards me - remember I am still just sitting there.  I again say to<BR>myself - please don't let it hit me (I find I'm doing a lot of talking to<BR>myself lately - :-)).  Well that didn't work and the Camry hit me and moved<BR>my front end 9 feet to the right (you know how light our front ends are).<BR>It wiped out the hood, windshield, fenders, front end, dent'd the metal<BR>support and I don't know what else.  My Fiero was cherry too - perfect<BR>condition, one year old paint job.  I was able to drive it home - for those<BR>of you complaining about the headlight doors opening at speeds above 130,<BR>try 55.  Anyway just had to tell someone who could appreciate my situation -<BR>sorry to anyone objecting to the bandwidth concerns.  PS my back and neck<BR>are sore, but can't complain there were three people from the Camry's 4 that<BR>went to the hospital.  Also if I hadn't been hit a long time ago similarly<BR>from someone running a red light, I would have been the one slammed into and<BR>considering he could have plowed into the driver's door - not something I<BR>want to think about.<BR>||||reg||8
