Z||000009||SloPonti||01-31-2000||12:01 AM||||hey i saw that car on ebay a while back ago! are you the seller or the buyer! i was very interested in that car but it was to far for me to drive to get it!<BR>sorry about your wrecked car! hope everything works out for you and the important thing is that you walked away from it! the car can be replaced but you can't! count your blessings! well sorry about the car!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000010||RickPierce||01-31-2000||01:09 AM||||Hi Sloponti,<P>I was the buyer - it was sweet and drove well.  It needed a brake job and I was planning to do the GrandAm/Beretta switch before the crash.  Well worth the $2500 - it was perfect and I only had about 100 miles on it since winning the auction - real bummer.  All my friends would stop me to tell me how sweet the ride was (like I needed to know ;-)).<P>Best, Rick||||reg||1
Z||000011||DRH||01-31-2000||01:36 AM||||Rick,<P>Insurance will most likely want to total it. You can negotiate though. Try to make sure the title stays in your name so you don't have to get a salvage on it. Try to get them to give what it's worth and let you keep it for what they can get for it (practically nothing, don't let them fool you). That may give you enough to have it fixed yourself.<P>Worth a try anyway... Don't let them fool you, they really aren't as concerned about a few thousand in property damage as they are about many times that in injury...<P>Good luck , David.||||reg||1
Z||000012||SloPonti||02-01-2000||12:34 AM||||well if i had got the car from ebay i wonder if it would still be wrecked! makes you wonder huh! anyways i am glad you got a good deal on the car-i like it very much! and i hope you get it back! did the wheels get damaged at all! if you parted it out you could make some money on it and get you a new one! just for thoughts!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000013||RickPierce||02-01-2000||08:17 AM||||No the wheels didn't get damaged.  After buying it the car had no suspension - those are 14" wheels w/ 50 series tires - the kid I bought it from had "skateboarded" the wheel setup.  Luckily I had the stocks as well and that returned it back to having some suspension (even w/ the Eibachs).  Still unsure what's the extent of the damage.||||reg||1
Z||000014||wkayl||02-03-2000||10:02 PM||||I know how you feel having your Fiero hit.  My son's 84 SE was hit by a guy running a stop sign on Jan 21st.  He didn't even stop to see if anyone was hurt.  They caught him about 20 min. after the accident (great piece of police work to follow the skid mark left by his bent front tire).  To see pictures of my son's car go to: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/crash.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/crash.html</A> <P>He just purchased a 86GT like mine (his is black, mine is red)<p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 02-04-2000).]||||reg||1
